        },
        {
          "name": "Shadowsickle",
          "type": "ex",
          "description": "An orchid snipper can attack with both of its claw attacks. If any of the claw attacks hit, add an additional 1d8 shadow damage per hit.",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Sudden Strike",
          "type": "ex",
          "description": "A mantis is particularly adept at moving quickly when its foes are surprised. During a surprise round, a giant mantis may act as if it had a full round to act, rather than just one standard action.",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "A giant praying mantis with a shiny silver body. The orchid snipper has a very rare body color among insect monsters, which makes its exoskeleton highly prized and very expensive. Many adventurers hunt them for their highly valued exoskeleton, but orchid snippers are much larger and more agile than humans, and their sickles are said to cleave solid steel in two, so very few are actually able to defeat them in battle."
